# Chat file paths — visibility on dark background

## Why HTML yellow often fails

Cursor’s agent chat **auto-detects** repo-looking paths and turns them into clickable `.md-clickable-code` links colored with `--cursor-text-link` (dark blue on black). That styling **overrides** agent-emitted `<span style="color:#FFEB3B">…</span>`, and `workbench.colorCustomizations` `textLink.foreground` does **not** change those chat links.

So an `.mdc` rule alone cannot force yellow file links in chat.

## What agents should still do

When listing changed files, prefer a short “Changes” list with full relative paths (no backticks if possible — backticks also get theme colors). Do not promise yellow HTML will render.

## Real fix (user UI, once)

Install the **Custom UI Style** extension, then in Cursor `settings.json`:

```json
"custom-ui-style.stylesheet": {
  ".md-clickable-code": "color: #FFEB3B !important;",
  ".markdown-root .md-clickable-code": "color: #FFEB3B !important;",
  ".markdown-root a": "color: #FFEB3B !important;",
  "a.ui-citation-link": "color: #FFEB3B !important;"
}
```

Then run **Custom UI Style: Reload**. After that, chat file paths (including auto-linked ones) show bright yellow.
